<title>FRANCE: France to propose Cr Lyonnais European sell-offs.</title>
<headline>France to propose Cr Lyonnais European sell-offs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French finance minister Jean Arthuis said on Sunday he would soon propose to the European Commission that state bank Credit Lyonnais sell &quot;certain, essentially European, establishments.&quot;</p>
<p>The French government is seeking the European Commission's approval for further state aid to the bank and the Commission in Brussels, which has the job of controlling state aid in the European Union, is looking for concessions in return.</p>
<p>Estimates of the total cost of bailing out Credit Lyonnais go as high as 130 billion francs but Arthuis, who was speaking on RTL radio, said it was impossible to say what the total cost would be at this stage.</p>
</text>
